  "notes": "Warm parchment UI (#f4efe4) with deep forest-green primary and a serif/sans pairing (Fraunces + Figtree). Each family member has a pastel colour that is used consistently in calendar chips, avatars and the night-strips (Marisol green, Elena terracotta, Tom blue, David lavender, Gloria magenta). Unfilled slots are drawn as amber diagonal-hatched dashed chips labelled 'Open', in the same yellow-hatch style the header coverage meters use for gaps. Every issue card in 'To sort out' explains the constraint reasoning in plain prose ('Elena doesn't do Tuesdays and Tom can't do weekdays') and offers a dark primary fix plus an outlined alternative; the top card is highlighted amber with a left accent bar. Clicking a slot (checked live) swaps the Family panel for a day panel that lists candidates with constraint reasons and their night-count impact ('4 → 5 nights'). Selecting a person greys out the days they cannot do and shows a dismissible filter chip. Calendar weeks run Sat–Fri, matching the rota start. Filed new-entry proposal 'suggested-fixes' for the To-sort-out issue/resolution queue."
